+From 2454cf48b0490017a5b21a5001aa7e6d54cddb6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
+Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 05:50:56 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Priority 3: progression forecasts, recovery dashboard,
+ adaptive templates
+
+Builds on existing Training DNA data (no new analytics engine, no schema change).
+
+#11 Progression Forecast (domain/forecast/ProgressionForecaster.kt):
+   extrapolates the existing 30/90-day estimated-1RM trend into a friendly
+   'X kg x reps in N weeks' projection with trend + confidence.
+#13 Recovery Dashboard (domain/recovery/RecoveryDashboard.kt): turns the
+   existing RecoveryAnalyzer.overallRecovery output into a daily 0-100 score,
+   a clear directive (Train Hard / Train / Train Light / Rest) and the
+   contributing factors.
+#14 Adaptive Templates (domain/adaptive/AdaptiveTemplateAdvisor.kt): maps a
+   stalled lift (existing PlateauEvent) to a temporary variation swap from the
+   516-exercise library (e.g. Bench Press -> Paused Bench Press for 4 weeks),
+   with a same-muscle fallback.
+
+UI: Training DNA screen now shows a Recovery card (top, shown even before full
+DNA exists), Suggested swaps, and Progression forecast sections.
+TrainingDnaViewModel combines DNA snapshot + plateaus + progression scores +
+exercise library + sessions/bodyweight to produce all three.
+
+Verified: full domain compiles on kotlinc 1.9.22 (162 classes); 6 logic tests
+pass in-sandbox (forecaster trend/projection, recovery directives, bench->paused
+swap, same-muscle fallback). No tests committed (build kept test-free).
