++## How to bring this into your repo
++
++A patch bundle is provided at `patches/replog-improvements.bundle` (a git bundle
++of `79debc5..eb48fee`). From a fresh clone of your repo on your machine:
++
++```bash
++# 1. Fetch the commits from the bundle into your clone
++git fetch /path/to/replog-improvements.bundle sync/apply-improvements
++
++# 2. Merge them onto main (fast-forward, since they sit on top of 79debc5)
++git checkout main
++git merge FETCH_HEAD          # or: git merge sync/apply-improvements
++
++# 3. Build & test, then push
++./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
++git push origin main
++```
++
++Alternatively, a flat patch file `patches/replog-improvements.patch` can be applied with
++`git apply` / `git am` if you prefer not to use the bundle.
